## Why
The strongest merger T for `fa consolidate` would be a Regulation S-X Article 11 pro forma condensed combined balance sheet, from an 8-K/A Exhibit 99 or an S-4 (docs/FORENSIC_CASE_STUDIES_PLAN.md §11.2). Its columns are acquirer historical + target historical + footnoted pro forma adjustments = pro forma combined. "No such filing was examined."

A bounded research bead must find and anchor one before any consolidation T is claimed. If none supports exact closure, consolidation is demonstrated only as a labelled scenario.

It serves claim type T: C3's **C-T-02**, the consolidation T id (§11.2), conditional on this bead. It is research: it closes with a decision record, and lands no expectation.

Exact closure is necessary but not sufficient. `fa consolidate` refuses an investment that is not the controlling share of capital, which includes one carrying goodwill: "Refused (exit 3, FA-REF-194): … an investment that is not the controlling share of capital (goodwill and pre-acquisition retained earnings are not modeled) …" (`registries/verbs.toml:640`; catalog row `registries/refusal_catalog.toml:1178`, `exit = "refusal"`, 3). A combination with PPA goodwill therefore cannot run C3 at 8196f5e40, and C2 records, for every candidate, whether its combination carries goodwill (§11.2).

## What to build
**Search.** Look in public EDGAR filings (8-K/A Exhibit 99, S-4) for an Article 11 pro forma condensed combined balance sheet.

**The decision record, in the merger case** (`crates/fa-oracles/cases/mergers/`):
- one `sources.toml` row per candidate examined (every §4.1 field, including `filed_on` read from the filing's EDGAR header at fetch and `restates`: `[]`, or the earlier filing an amendment such as an 8-K/A or an S-4/A supersedes for the same pro forma table, so K-VINTAGE can force the latest vintage; `status = OK` with the SHA-256 of the captured bytes once retrieved, else `BLOCKED` with its `status_reason`), whose `notes` record: accession, document and retrieval route; the closure class from the check below; whether the adjustments are footnoted with amounts sourced in the filing; the assurance status of the pro forma information; and the **consolidation shape** against FA-REF-194's preconditions: whether the combination carries goodwill (with its amount), whether the acquirer's investment equals the controlling share of the target's contributed capital (no pre-acquisition retained earnings eliminated against it), whether the stake is whole basis points, and how many entities and intercompany balances it needs (`registries/verbs.toml:640`); and which printed combined lines are whole-type totals (total assets, total liabilities, total equity, total liabilities and equity), the only lines `fa consolidate`'s balance sheet reports, so the only lines C3 can claim (its balance sheet is the embedded type-level `balance-sheet` definition, `crates/fa-statements/src/concordat.rs:1988`; §3.8);
- for the selected filing only: its line facts in `facts.toml` (`sourced`, `granularity = statement_line`, `anchor_kind = table_cell`, `anchor = <table>|<row label>|<column label>` (A1a's grammar), `cell = "<line>:<column>@<date>"` (the column label separates the acquirer, target, each adjustment and the combined value, as X1's member separates A, Δ and B: four columns sharing `<line>@<date>` would let K-VINTAGE compare a restating filing's combined value with another column's fact, A3b), the acquirer, target, each adjustment and the combined value committed as `[[value]]` rows, plus a `scale{multiplier}` derived fact from the table's unit legend), the sourced fact its row's `assurance` names as A1a's `assurance_fact` (the filing's sentence or legend stating the pro forma information's assurance, prose-anchored, so the row's `anchor_scheme` adds `line` or `page` and that fact's receipt has `alignment = "sentence"`; a candidate with no committed facts records its assurance in `notes` only), and their receipts from `case_fetch.py verify` (§4.4: `alignment = "value"`, all four binding booleans `quote_found_once`, `aligned`, `values_in_quote`, `scope_ok` true, `values_sha256` over the committed values and scope, and `original_hash_compared` copied from the source row; `table_cell` facts bind by exact printed value, §4.1 as amended);
- the bead's close reason names the selected accession; or states that a filing closes exactly but carries goodwill (or another FA-REF-194 shape), so C-T-02 needs a `fa consolidate` capability first (a product bead filed with that filing as its oracle, §13) and consolidation is demonstrated meanwhile only as a labelled scenario; or states that none closes exactly and that consolidation is demonstrated only as a labelled scenario.

**The closure check** (a fa-oracles function, `classify_pro_forma(lines, display_unit) -> per line Exact | WithinDisplayBand | Fails`, exact checked integer arithmetic): a line is `Exact` when acquirer + target + Σ adjustments = combined at the printed precision, `WithinDisplayBand` when they differ by no more than one display unit (rounding), and `Fails` otherwise. A filing is selectable for C3 only if every line is `Exact` **and** its recorded consolidation shape is one `fa consolidate` admits (no goodwill, investment = the controlling share of contributed capital, whole-basis-point stake). A candidate with any `WithinDisplayBand` line and no `Fails` line is recorded C-only and never selected for a T. An all-`Exact` candidate with goodwill is recorded `exact_not_consolidatable{FA-REF-194: goodwill}` and never selected; it is the oracle a later `fa consolidate` goodwill capability would use. Candidates are classified at authoring from the capture; the selected filing is re-classified offline from its committed facts. A second pure function `selectable_for_c3(closure, shape) -> Selected | CloseOnly | ExactNotConsolidatable(reason)` encodes the rule.

**Access.** `python3 -B tools/case-fetch/case_fetch.py fetch|extract|verify mergers`, the project User-Agent for every request, archive captures unless `FA_SEC_CONTACT` is set (OD 1), and the cache outside the repo (§4.3).

