## Why

Product finding H6 (docs/FORENSIC_CASE_STUDIES_PLAN.md §13; §8.3 L-N-01): no registered law refuses a repo recharacterized as a sale; there is no derecognition or repurchase law. The documented accounting form is Appendix 17 p.8: "The re‐characterization entry is: Dr. Repo $100 / Dr. Long inventory‐derivative $5 / Cr. Inventory $105", a 3-leg entry (§8.2). The case publishes L-N-01 with equal prominence (§0.3). At 8196f5e40 no law-level twin exists for it: Canon rules turn recorded events into legs, and "Rule families bound to intents are not in this build" (`registries/verbs.toml:664`), so no planted rule can refuse a posted intent. L-N-01 therefore carries a harness-observability twin (the same entry in a Closed period is refused `FA-REF-010`, §8.3a), and L4 does not wait on H6. §13 frames H6 as research: "a kernel law, an intent-bound Canon rule family, or a Lantern detector? Whichever lands flips L-N-01 and gives it a law-level twin."

## What to build

A research decision record that answers:
